      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The opponent controls Lion's Eye Diamond and Mox Opal, but Mox Opal's metalcraft is not active (only 2 artifacts: LED and Mox Opal). However, the player has Back to Basics in hand which would lock down the opponent's nonbasic lands (Underground Sea, Badlands). Destroying Lion's Eye Diamond with Flame of Anor is reasonable since LED enables explosive turns (Beseech the Mirror combos), but the player chose to destroy an artifact without drawing cards. Since they don't control a Wizard, they can only choose ONE mode. Choosing 'Destroy target artifact' to hit LED is defensible, but choosing 'Target player draws two cards' to draw 2 cards would likely be stronger here. LED is a combo piece but the opponent already has it on board and could activate it in response to Flame of Anor (discarding hand to add mana as an instant). Since LED can be activated in response, the destroy mode may not even successfully deny the opponent the LED's mana - they can just crack it for mana before it resolves. Drawing 2 cards would be guaranteed value and help find more interaction. The opponent can simply sacrifice LED in response, making the destroy mode potentially worthless.",
